    "ImageDescription": {
      "value": "\"Painting on paper depicting the white-complexioned Nandi in his zoo-anthropomorphic form.\nNandi is standing on a low pedestal. He wears a crown, is dressed in a dhoti and an angavstra is draped on his elbows, on his forehead, chest and arms are tripundra marks. In his upper right hand he carries the parashu, in his upper left the mriga. In his lower right hand is a long rod topped with a crouching Nandi image, his lower left hand hangs at his side.\"",
